    "markdown": "---\nengine: knitr\n---\n\n# Recap\n![](/images/question_bubble_red.png){style=\"width:150px\" fig-align=\"center\"}\n\nBrilliant! You've gone through all the advanced Linux practice.\nThe next page contains an exercise.\nBefore that there is a little information on permissions followed by some recap MCQs.\n\n\n## Permissions\nAll files, directories and programs have permissions. It is important to know about this so you know your read, write and executability permissions for the content within machines.\n\nBelow is a useful link to learn about file permissions:  \n<https://www.guru99.com/file-permissions.html>\n\n## MCQs\n\nPlease attempt to answer the below Multiple-Choice Questions to reinforce what you have learnt in this part.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n1.  Which symbol is used to pipe the output of one command to the input of another? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_XXAREYNLDJ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_XXAREYNLDJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_XXAREYNLDJ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_XXAREYNLDJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n2.  What command can be used to substitute text with other text? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_AWDCZBGFGZ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_AWDCZBGFGZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_AWDCZBGFGZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_AWDCZBGFGZ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n3.  Which symbol is used to redirect the output of a command to a file? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_CJQSEAMXMB'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CJQSEAMXMB\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CJQSEAMXMB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CJQSEAMXMB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n4. Which wildcard represents a single character? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_WKKRTZUWPZ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_WKKRTZUWPZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_WKKRTZUWPZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_WKKRTZUWPZ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n5. Which wildcard represents zero or more characters? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_IJKKIOAYNB'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IJKKIOAYNB\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IJKKIOAYNB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IJKKIOAYNB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n6. Which wildcard represents a range of characters? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_TSLZAVNAVR'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TSLZAVNAVR\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TSLZAVNAVR\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TSLZAVNAVR\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n7. Which regular expression indicates that the preceding character matches 1 or 0 times? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_TDHHRGNANX'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TDHHRGNANX\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TDHHRGNANX\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_TDHHRGNANX\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n8. Which regular expression represents a single character?  <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_JJNPRXWXWM'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JJNPRXWXWM\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JJNPRXWXWM\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JJNPRXWXWM\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n9. Which regular expression indicates that the preceding character matches zero or more times? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_SRDCKZEXPQ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SRDCKZEXPQ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SRDCKZEXPQ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SRDCKZEXPQ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n10. Which regular expression matches the end of the line? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_UUFNRRVRMB'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UUFNRRVRMB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UUFNRRVRMB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UUFNRRVRMB\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n11. Which regular expression is a logical OR operator? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_KLHEQOAMPP'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KLHEQOAMPP\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KLHEQOAMPP\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KLHEQOAMPP\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n12. Which regular expression matches the start of the line? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_SXMBYVYSDF'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SXMBYVYSDF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SXMBYVYSDF\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SXMBYVYSDF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n",
